==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|kipe}}, {{m|enm|kype}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cȳpe}}, {{m|ang|cȳpa||basket}}, akin to {{cog|gml|kīpe}} {{gloss|"basket"; > {{cog|nds-de|Kiep}}, {{m|nds-de|Kiepke||basket}}, {{cog|de|Kiepe}}}}, {{cog|no|kaup||wooden box; crate}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[Image:Chittenden Locks - salmon in ladder 4216.jpg|thumb|250 px|A salmon with the beginnings of a kipe as it enters fresh water.]]

# An [[osier]] basket used for catching fish.
# Upturned lower jaw of a male [[salmon]] at the end of its life as it returns to fresh water to [[spawn]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|kip}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} to [[steal]]

